  "faqSignalsQ1": "What are Avexa signals?",
  "faqSignalsA1": "Avexa signals are trading opportunities generated from market data and analysis. Each signal can include information such as entry price, take profit, stop loss and market direction.",
  "faqSignalsQ2": "How often are new signals released?",
  "faqSignalsA2": "The number of available signals depends on your Avexa plan. Free users have limited access, while PRO users receive access to additional premium signals.",
  "faqSignalsQ3": "What do Entry, TP and SL mean?",
  "faqSignalsA3": "Entry is the suggested price or price range for entering a trade. TP (Take Profit) represents the target where the trade may be closed for profit. SL (Stop Loss) represents the level where the trade may be closed to limit potential losses.",
  "faqSignalsQ4": "Are Avexa signals guaranteed to be profitable?",
  "faqSignalsA4": "No. No trading signal can guarantee a profit. Signals are based on analysis and available market data, but cryptocurrency markets are volatile and every trade carries risk.",
  "faqSignalsQ5": "Where can I see my available signals?",
  "faqSignalsA5": "Your available signals can be found in the Signals section of Avexa. Access and availability depend on your current plan.",

  "faqProQ1": "What is Avexa PRO?",
  "faqProA1": "Avexa PRO is the premium version of Avexa. It provides access to additional trading intelligence, premium signals and advanced features that are not available on the Free plan.",
  "faqProQ2": "How do I upgrade to PRO?",
  "faqProA2": "Open your Subscription screen and select Upgrade to PRO. Follow the payment instructions to complete your subscription.",
  "faqProQ3": "How do I know if I have PRO?",
  "faqProA3": "You can check your current plan in your Profile or Subscription screen. PRO accounts will show an active PRO membership.",
  "faqProQ4": "Can I cancel my PRO subscription?",
  "faqProA4": "Yes. You can manage or cancel your subscription from the Subscription screen. Your access may remain active until the end of your current billing period.",
  "faqProQ5": "What happens when my PRO subscription expires?",
  "faqProA5": "When your PRO access expires, your account returns to the Free plan and premium features become unavailable until PRO is activated again.",

  "faqTradingQ1": "What is a Take Profit (TP)?",
  "faqTradingA1": "Take Profit is a predefined target price. When the market reaches that level, a trader may choose to close the position and secure the planned profit.",
  "faqTradingQ2": "What is a Stop Loss (SL)?",
  "faqTradingA2": "Stop Loss is a predefined level used to limit potential losses if the market moves against the trade.",
  "faqTradingQ3": "What is an Entry?",
  "faqTradingA3": "Entry is the price or price range where the signal suggests considering opening a position.",
  "faqTradingQ4": "Why can my result differ from the signal?",
  "faqTradingA4": "Market prices can change very quickly. Slippage, execution speed, liquidity and fees can cause your actual entry or exit price to differ from the price shown in a signal.",
  "faqTradingQ5": "Does Avexa execute trades automatically?",
  "faqTradingA5": "Avexa signals are designed to provide trading intelligence. Unless a specific automated trading feature is enabled and supported, you remain responsible for executing and managing your trades.",

  "faqAccountQ1": "How do I change my username?",
  "faqAccountA1": "Open Profile and select Personal Information. From there you can update the information associated with your profile.",
  "faqAccountQ2": "How do I change my password?",
  "faqAccountA2": "Open Profile → Security and use the available password management options.",
  "faqAccountQ3": "Can I change my email address?",
  "faqAccountA3": "Email account changes should be handled through the account security settings when the option is available. Additional verification may be required.",
  "faqAccountQ4": "How do I log out?",
  "faqAccountA4": "Open your Profile and scroll to the bottom of the screen. Select LOG OUT to end your current session.",
  "faqAccountQ5": "Can I delete my account?",
  "faqAccountA5": "Account deletion can be requested through the account or security section. Make sure you understand that deleting an account may permanently remove associated data.",

  "faqNotificationsQ1": "How do I enable notifications?",
  "faqNotificationsA1": "Open More → App Settings → Notifications. From there you can control general notifications, signal alerts and haptic feedback.",
  "faqNotificationsQ2": "What are Signal Alerts?",
  "faqNotificationsA2": "Signal Alerts notify you when a new relevant trading signal becomes available.",
  "faqNotificationsQ3": "Why am I not receiving notifications?",
  "faqNotificationsA3": "First check that notifications are enabled in Avexa Settings and in your device settings. Also make sure Signal Alerts are enabled if you want to receive signal notifications.",
  "faqNotificationsQ4": "What is Haptic Feedback?",
  "faqNotificationsA4": "Haptic Feedback uses your device vibration to provide additional feedback for supported interactions and alerts.",

